# ── SG16 AI Engine — build-time configuration ────────────────────────────
# The app is a universal AI gateway: there is no backend server and no list
# of known providers. You give it a raw API base URL, an optional API key,
# and model strings — any endpoint that speaks the standard
# chat-completions protocol works. The variables below are optional
# build-time defaults; the Admin panel (/admin) configures connections at
# runtime and stores them on the device.
#
# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and fill in what you need.

# --- Default AI endpoint (optional) ---------------------------------------
# Any raw endpoint URL, e.g. https://api.example.com/v1
# VITE_SG16_AI_BASE_URL=
# A label shown in the Admin panel:
# VITE_SG16_AI_NAME=
# API key for the endpoint (kept in the built app — prefer runtime Admin setup):
# VITE_SG16_AI_API_KEY=
# Model slots (the chat model is required for a usable connection):
# VITE_SG16_AI_MODEL=
# VITE_SG16_AI_CODING_MODEL=
# VITE_SG16_AI_VISION_MODEL=

# --- Live web search ------------------------------------------------------
# 1 (default): time-sensitive questions get live news/web context via the
# edge functions (/api/edge/news, /api/edge/search). Set to 0 to disable.
# VITE_SG16_LIVE_SEARCH=1

# --- Local development ----------------------------------------------------
# `npm run dev` serves only the SPA. To test the edge functions locally:
#   npm run build && npx wrangler pages dev dist
# Deploy: connect this repo to Cloudflare Pages (build command: npm run build,
# output directory: dist) — the functions/ directory is deployed automatically.
